  "summary": "Genomic data sharing and synthetic expression data generation are being benchmarked and audited for privacy leakage before release.",
  "synthesis": "Three items address privacy-preserving handling of genomic data, and the dominant thread is controlling disclosure risk before data leave their custodians. Two preprints from 2026-11-13 apply epsilon-local differential privacy: one offers a PCA-based pre-release auditing framework that quantifies membership inference risk in genomic data sharing while accounting for attacker auxiliary information, and the other offers a privacy-preserving framework for server-side selection of clustering methods and hyperparameters for population stratification using distributed PCA. The published benchmark from 2026-11-09 takes a different route, evaluating 11 generative methods for privacy-preserving synthetic bulk RNA-seq across two cancer cohorts of about 1,000 and 5,000 patients and 978 landmark genes, with fidelity among the assessed properties. The new element is privacy protection extended to collaborative stratification and synthetic transcriptomic release, not only to raw data sharing.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-haiku-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-18"
}
